# Grafana Webhook Alerting for High-Severity Alerts

## Task Summary
Configured [Grafana](http://localhost:3000) alerting so that alerts with the label `severity=high` route to the webhook sink endpoint `http://webhook-sink:5000/hook`.

## Provisioning Actions Performed

### 1. Created Webhook Contact Point
Endpoint: `POST http://admin:grafana2026@localhost:3000/api/v1/provisioning/contact-points`

```json
{
  "name": "webhook-oncall",
  "type": "webhook",
  "settings": {
    "url": "http://webhook-sink:5000/hook",
    "httpMethod": "POST"
  }
}
Response:

JSON
{
  "uid": "cg4tmxokn01s0d",
  "name": "webhook-oncall",
  "type": "webhook",
  "settings": {
    "httpMethod": "POST",
    "url": "http://webhook-sink:5000/hook"
  },
  "disableResolveMessage": false
}
2. Updated Notification Policy Tree
Endpoint: PUT http://admin:grafana2026@localhost:3000/api/v1/provisioning/policies

Preserved existing root receiver "empty" and added a route matching severity = high to receiver "webhook-oncall".

JSON
{
  "receiver": "empty",
  "group_by": [
    "grafana_folder",
    "alertname"
  ],
  "routes": [
    {
      "receiver": "webhook-oncall",
      "object_matchers": [
        [
          "severity",
          "=",
          "high"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
Response:

JSON
{"message":"policies updated"}
Verification
Bash
curl -s http://admin:grafana2026@localhost:3000/api/v1/provisioning/contact-points | jq
curl -s http://admin:grafana2026@localhost:3000/api/v1/provisioning/policies | jq
EOF
